      "value": "@{654a7d1f1870ff9faf0911e8|full_name} this is absolutely better but still WAY off from where it needs to be.\n\nThe keyboard should be exactly where my POV is facing, no matter if I'm laying down or standing up. I'm sure this look normal to people when they are standing up but when they are laying down I have to try to find my keyboard or guess where it is to move it to a place where I can actually see it. This means I'm going to have to keep trying to search for it EVERY SINGLE TIME I need to re-open the textbox which is not good for someone who is disabled, like me.\n\nAnother thing is that because they are separated that's two things I need to keep track of. Why not add a button that merges the two UI together? That way I can save that I want my input to be tracked to my keyboard and just drag the WHOLE thing if I need to whenever.\n\nThe other issue is that the keyboard/input field is ONLY draggable from the title of the UI box rather than the ENTIRE UI box which means I have to be very accurate when moving the box. Again, this is awful for people who are disabled if I:\n\n1. Have to FIND the box.\n\n2. Have to then find EXACTLY the title, and thus have to move or try to scooch down more from laying down just to try to grab the title when I physically cannot see it.\n\nI included a video of me struggling with the chatbox. Though it IS much more usable now, it's still WAY off than where it needs to be vs the old keyboard that worked just fine.\n\nTL;DR:\n\nWorks better, still off. Add a button that merges the two UI's (input and keyboard) into one. Make entire thing draggable. Appear from POV facing rather than hips it seems? Save that location so a user doesn't have to keep grabbing TWO UIs to try to see what they are typing when they can't see the UI at all when laying down. An option for the old keyboard would much rather be preferred. Needs more accessibility in mind when developing this new UI.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
